 ## Operating characteristics
 
 ### Time and Memory Complexity
-*   **Time:** The method uses least squares fitting, which is computationally more intensive than fast spherical harmonic transforms due to the lack of special sampling points in standard MRI hardware [S1]. The complexity depends on the number of gradient directions $N$ and the number of coefficients $K$ (which grows with order $r$). Solving the linear system is $O(N K^2)$ or $O(N K)$ depending on the solver [G].
-*   **Memory:** Requires storing the gradient directions, b-values, and the resulting coefficients for each voxel. Higher orders require more coefficients per voxel [S1].
